    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (3/3 tests, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional `postcode` support for owner creation, validated only when present.\n\n**What was added/changed:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` property (`^[0-9]{4}$`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` extends `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto` both gain `postcode`, so it's accepted on create and returned on read.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 Added a `postcode` column field with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name automatically (no mapper change needed) for both request\u2192entity and entity\u2192response.\n\n3. **Schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `postcode` column so the field persists. Tests run against hsqldb.\n\n4. **`ValidateOwnerPostcode`** function \u2014 A new pipeline step that validates the postcode **only when present**:\n   - `null` (absent) \u2192 skipped, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n   - Not exactly 4 digits \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n   - City with a known region (via the existing `Locality` table: Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) \u2192 must fall in NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099, else 400.\n   - City with no known region \u2192 any 4-digit postcode accepted.\n\n5. **`InvalidPostcodeException` + handler + escalation YAML** \u2014 Following the existing `InvalidTelephoneException` pattern, responds 400 with the field error.\n\n6. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Wired `validatePostcode` immediately after required-field validation, so a bad postcode is rejected before any persistence work.\n\n**Tests:** `coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, and `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode` all pass, and the full suite is green.",
